    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0995" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg845"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4500/41–42.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Thompson
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-12-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 18, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 843.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 837, of the
                    15th instant, I acknowledge the receipt of your telegram of yesterday’s date on
                    the <pb facs="0996" n="846" xml:id="pg846"/> subject of the reciprocal
                    advantages required by Mexico contingent to granting permission for the American
                    Government to station two coaling barges in Magdalena Bay, as follows:<anchor
                        n="a" xml:id="d239-f1"/></p>
                <p>A copy of my note which was sent to the foreign office on receipt of of the above
                    telegram is inclosed herewith. This note was addressed to Mr. Algara,
                    subsecretary for foreign affairs, who is at present in charge of that
                    department, Mr. Mariscal being ill and away from the city.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. E. Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d239-a1.xml" xpointer="d239-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
